Relevant columns / possible usages
• GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_BOUNDARIES.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_WAYS  
  "id": unique identifier that will let us join the same table to itself (pairs of roads).  
  "geometry": the GEOMETRY object that we will pass to ST_INTERSECTS to see whether two roads overlap and to check whether a road sits inside California.  
  "all_tags": JSON array – flatten it to find `highway=*` (motorway, trunk, primary, secondary, residential) and to be sure no `bridge=*` tag exists.  
  "nodes": JSON array with node‑ids; flatten two ways and verify they do not share a common node.  

• GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.STATES  
  "state_geom": California polygon that will be intersected with road geometries.  
  "state": two–letter code; "CA" will be used in WHERE clause to pull only the California geometry.  

Typical filter conditions we will eventually need
1.  FLATTEN(all_tags) AS t  …  WHERE t.value:"key"::STRING = 'highway'  
                               AND t.value:"value"::STRING IN ('motorway','trunk','primary','secondary','residential')
2.  NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM LATERAL FLATTEN(input => w.all_tags) f WHERE f.value:"key"::STRING = 'bridge')
3.  ST_INTERSECTS(w.geometry , ca.state_geom)
4.  ST_INTERSECTS(w1.geometry , w2.geometry)  AND  w1.id < w2.id
5.  ARRAY_INTERSECTION(ARRAY_AGG(n1.value::NUMBER), ARRAY_AGG(n2.value::NUMBER)) IS NULL   -- no shared nodes  

